# Branch-scoped issue review

For **check for issues**, **code review**, **review for problems**, **audit the branch**, **review this branch**, **review this PR**, **PR review**, or similar: follow the personal Agent Skill **`branch-issue-review`** (`~/.cursor/skills/branch-issue-review/SKILL.md`). Use **only** the **current workspace git repository**—do not search sibling repos or paths outside `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`.

## Preconditions (always enforce)

1. **Clean tree** (branch-vs-base only): `git status --porcelain` must be empty or **stop** (commit/stash/discard first). **Exception:** uncommitted / working-tree / staged review—see skill **Working-tree review**.

2. **Fetch / pull** (branch-vs-base only): **`git fetch origin`** (or **`git fetch --all --prune`** when multiple remotes matter). Then **`git pull`** when the current branch has an upstream—**stop** if pull conflicts. Then resolve branch checkout from extra message text if applicable. **Exception:** **Working-tree review**—skip fetch/pull.

3. **Extra text names a branch:** Text beyond the review phrase → **`git checkout`** that ref (try **`origin/<name>`** after fetch). Example: `code review issue/PROJ-1234` → checkout `issue/PROJ-1234`, then `origin/issue/PROJ-1234` if needed. Invalid ref → **stop**.

If the user listed **only** exact paths, skip branch diff steps **but still** apply preconditions **1-3** above when they used branch-review phrasing (**code review**, **review this branch**, etc.) **without** working-tree scope. **Working-tree review** takes precedence when both appear.

All workflow steps (branch diff, working-tree diff, workspace rules, large-diff policy, report, test/CI awareness, `unless` severity) and **Reporting conventions** live in the **`branch-issue-review`** skill—open it and follow it end-to-end.
